<title>RUSSIA: Russian energy giant futures open in St Petersburg.</title>
<headline>Russian energy giant futures open in St Petersburg.</headline>
<dateline>ST PETERSBURG, Russia 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Daily trade in futures of Russian power utility UES, natural gas monopoly Gazprom and oil company LUKoil started on Wednesday on the St Petersburg Exchange, Clearing Centre deputy head Alexei Sergeyev said.</p>
<p>Futures in regional energy company Mosenergo, international long-distance provider Rostelekom and metals concern Norilsk Nickel already trade on the Russian Exchange.</p>
<p>The Russian Exchange recently launched a futures contract on the Russian Trading System index also, while futures are also traded on the Siberian Stock Exchange in Novosibirsk.</p>
<p>The minimum accepted futures contract for UES on the St Petersburg Exchange is 10,000 shares, for Gazprom 1,000 shares and for LUKoil, 100 shares.</p>
<p>Over 25 participants are currently registered on the futures trading floor.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
